    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0510" n="1244" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1244"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 471.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 414, of
                    the 8th ultimo, I inclose herewith a copy of a communication addressed by the
                    commander in chief of the United States naval force on the European station to
                    the Secretary of the Navy, and by him communicated to this Department with a
                    letter of the 14th instant, embodying the result of his observations during the
                    recent visit of the U. S, S. <hi rendition="#italic">San Francisco</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> to Turkish waters.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d508-a1.xml" xpointer="d508-a1"/>
